{
    "name": "E2E Utils Controls - Each sequential order",
    "description": "Iterates [1200, 50, 600, 10] with Each in Sequential mode. The loop body busy-waits that many milliseconds per item (so a plain Each lets the fast items overtake the slow ones) and then confirms the item with Continue Each. JoinEach collects the results in ARRIVAL order and the Assert requires the original order. The body also reads a variable of a component BEFORE Each, which proves the engine restores the original message scope for items 1..N (they are emitted from a webhook delivery, not from the 'in' message). Continue Each also adds the result of each item to the loop's Result, and a second Assert on the 'done' port requires that list to hold all four values in item order.",
